To set up Auth0 SSO (Single Sign-On) for multiple React apps, follow these steps:

1. Sign up for an Auth0 account and create a new application.
2. In the Auth0 dashboard, navigate to the "Applications" tab and click on your newly created application.
3. Under the "Settings" tab, click on "SSO" and enable the "SAML 2.0" protocol.
4. Click on the "Create SAML 2.0 Metadata" button to download the metadata file.
5. Install the `@auth0/auth0-react` library in your React apps using npm or yarn:
```bash
npm install @auth0/auth0-react
```
or
```bash
yarn add @auth0/auth0-react
```
6. Create a new file called `Auth0Provider.js` in your React apps and import the necessary libraries:
```javascript
import { Auth0Provider } from '@auth0/auth0-react';
```
7. In the `Auth0Provider.js` file, define the Auth0 configuration object and pass it to the `Auth0Provider` component:
```javascript
const auth0Config = {
  domain: 'your-domain.com',
  clientId: 'your-client-id',
  redirectUri: 'http://localhost:3000/callback',
};

function Auth0ProviderWrapper({ children }) {
  return (
    <Auth0Provider
      {...auth0Config}
      onRedirectCallback={(appState) => {
        if (appState && appState.error) {
          console.error(appState.error);
        }
      }}
    >
      {children}
    </Auth0Provider>
  );
}

export default Auth0ProviderWrapper;
```
Replace `your-domain.com` with your Auth0 domain and `your-client-id` with your Auth0 client ID.
