It seems like you want to distribute the planets evenly in the canvas. Here's an updated version of your `generateRandomPlanets` function that ensures the distance between each planet is greater than the minimum distance:

```javascript
const generateRandomPlanets = (numPlanets, minDistance) => {
  const planets = [];
  let attempts = 0;

  while (planets.length < numPlanets && attempts < 100) {
    attempts++;

    const planet = {
      position: [
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
        randomPosition(-30, 30),
      ],
      size: randomSize(1, 5) * scale,
      color: randomColor(),
      ringSize: 0.2 * scale,
      ringColor: randomColor(),
      ringNoise: 0.3 * scale,
    };

    let valid = true;

    for (let i = 0; i < planets.length; i++) {
      const distance = planet.position.reduce((a, b) => a + b * b, 0);

      if (distance < minDistance * minDistance) {
        valid = false;
        break;
      }
    }

    if (valid) {
      planets.push(planet);
    }
  }

  return planets;
};
```

This function will randomly generate planets until it has generated the desired number of planets or reached the maximum number of attempts. It will then check if the distance between each planet is greater than the minimum distance. If it is not, it will generate a new planet at a different location. This process will continue until all the planets are evenly distributed in the canvas.

Here's a simple React utility that removes widows from a given text. Widows refer to the last line of a paragraph that is significantly shorter than the other lines, making it look unbalanced. This utility splits the text into sentences, checks for widows, and joins the sentences back together with appropriate line breaks.

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ text }) => {
  const [widowedText, setWidowedText] = useState(text);

  const handleRemoveWidows = () => {
    const sentences = widowedText.split('.');
    const newSentences = [];

    for (let i = 0; i < sentences.length; i++) {
      const sentence = sentences[i];
      const words = sentence.split(' ');

      if (words.length > 1) {
        const lastWord = words[words.length - 1];
        const lastWordLength = lastWord.length;

        if (lastWordLength < 5) {
          // Add a line break before the last word
          newSentences.push(`${sentence} \n`);
        } else {
          // Join the words back together
          newSentences.push(sentence);
        }
      }
    }

    setWidowedText(newSentences.join('.'));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <button onClick={handleRemoveWidows}>Remove Widows</button>
      <pre>{widowedText}</pre>
    </div>
  );
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

