To create an iOS shortcut that identifies and deletes user files that haven't been accessed in over 3 years, follow these steps:

1. Open the Shortcuts app on your iPhone or iPad.
2. Tap on "Create Shortcut" at the bottom of the screen.
3. Give your shortcut a name, for example, "Delete Old Files."
4. Add the following actions to the shortcut:
   a. "Get Contents of [Folder]" - Set the folder to "Photos," "Documents," or any other folder where you want to check for old files.
   b. "Filter Items" - Add a filter to only show items that have not been accessed in over 3 years. You can use the "Modification Date" variable and set the date range to 3 years ago.
   c. "Remove Items" - Add an action to remove the selected items. Make sure to confirm the removal before proceeding.
5. Test your shortcut by running it on a test device or a backup of your device.
6. Once you're satisfied with the shortcut, save it and share it with others if you wish.

Here's a sample shortcut JSON code:
```json
